                                    <h1>No-Code + Low-Code for Enterprise: Where It Actually Works in 2026</h1>
                                    <p>No-code and low-code platforms have real production value in 2026 — but they're not the 'replace developers' hype from 2020. Here is where they actually earn their keep, where they fail, and how they compare to custom builds.</p>
                                    <h2>Where No-Code / Low-Code Genuinely Wins</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Internal tools + admin dashboards:</strong> Retool, Airplane, Superblocks. 5-10x faster than custom for internal use.<br><strong>Simple customer-facing sites / landing pages:</strong> Webflow, Framer, Wix.<br><strong>Workflow automation:</strong> n8n, Zapier, Make.<br><strong>Simple business apps:</strong> Bubble, Adalo for early-stage prototypes.<br><strong>Enterprise app modernization:</strong> Mendix, OutSystems, Microsoft Power Apps for wrapping legacy systems.</p>
                                    <h2>Where They Fail</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Complex customer-facing products with performance-critical requirements.</strong> Load, custom features, complex data models — no-code hits walls.<br><strong>Deep integration workflows.</strong> Sooner or later you'll need custom code anyway.<br><strong>Cost at scale.</strong> Per-user pricing on no-code platforms compounds; at 100+ users, custom often cheaper over 3 years.<br><strong>Vendor lock-in.</strong> Moving off Bubble / Retool is painful; plan for it upfront.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost Comparison</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Retool / Airplane internal tool:</strong> $12-40/user/month + build time.<br><strong>Custom equivalent:</strong> ₹15-40 lakh build + hosting. Payback period vs Retool: 2-4 years typically.<br><strong>Mendix / OutSystems enterprise:</strong> $50-200/user/month.<br><strong>Custom Django / Node equivalent:</strong> ₹80 lakh - 3 Cr initial + ongoing team.</p>
                                    <h2>Enterprise Reality</h2>
                                    <p>Governance matters more than tool choice. Without a shared registry, ownership rules, and quality standards, no-code / low-code sprawl silently becomes worse than the legacy systems it replaced.</p>
                                    <h2>Regional Notes</h2>
                                    <p><strong>India:</strong> Custom-build talent is abundant + cheap, making no-code less compelling for many workloads.<br><strong>UAE:</strong> Government + banking pushing low-code (Mendix, OutSystems) for internal apps.<br><strong>USA:</strong> Retool + Airtable + Zapier dominant in growth-stage companies.<br><strong>UK:</strong> Financial services adopting low-code for internal ops.<br><strong>Australia:</strong> Similar to USA pattern.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
                                        <h3 style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:15px;">Ready to Get Started?</h3>
